er/Armor. I'm actually considering an essence upgrade to GSS that gives it an indefinite duration (And explicitly state that it's a valid target for weapon summoning) so that it can actually be someone's main weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I tried to copy those Charms pretty closely. And I like the idea of letting GSS become indefinite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T00:56:38-08:00","id":825311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>norraba</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=823953#post823953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> stop trying to force me to take strength lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you even lift, bro? <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=824001#post824001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is everybody here in the same game?<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it's just Norraba and I from my group. Unless one of my other players is deciding to lurk in here without my knowledge.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I got bored and had time on my hands, so I made a pdf of your rewrite and charms. Mostly so I can have it at my table, but someone else might find it useful too. If it's alright with you, I can post a link to it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1067-primefactorx01","name":"Primefactorx01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1067_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T16:07:51-08:00","id":825640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primefactorx01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=825311#post825311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure it's just Norraba and I from my group. Unless one of my other players is deciding to lurk in here without my knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Coulda sworn your first post was from someone else. Did you change your avatar?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primefactorx01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=825311#post825311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I got bored and had time on my hands, so I made a pdf of your rewrite and charms. Mostly so I can have it at my table, but someone else might find it useful too. If it's alright with you, I can post a link to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be great!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T19:27:01-08:00","id":825713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=825640#post825640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh. Coulda sworn your first post was from someone else. Did you change your avatar?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That'd be great!</div> </div> </div> </div>I did at one point. It may have been between posts in this thread.<br /> <br /> Link to said <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/6a6kow29p67gsnd/Sanctaphrax%27s%20Craft%20Rewrite.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">PDF</a>.<br /> It comes to 11 pages. (Well, 9 and a quarter pages + index), at 9 pt font, single spaced, double column. There's some tweaking to be done (double quotation marks may look weird. may have missed a comment here and there, and so on.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1067,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1067-primefactorx01","user":"Primefactorx01","date":". 02-07-2016, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1067-primefactorx01","name":"Primefactorx01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1067_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T01:00:36-08:00","id":825830,"title":"","content":"Very nice!<br /> <br /> Thanks for making it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T01:47:19-08:00","id":842924,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry if this has already been posted earlier somewhere, but I've been workshopping Craft fixes with my party's Twilight and wanted to post this charm I hope to test soon:<br /> <br /> <i>Limitless Insight Practice</i><br /> Cost - Craft 5 Essence 1<br /> Permanent, Stackable<br /> Chains Fall Away, Craftsman Needs No Tools<br /> The Solar craftsmen is a bottomless font of creativity, but only fools assume that they are done learning. This charm may be purchased once for every Craft ability the Solar possesses at five dots (or Craft specialty under the rewrite), allowing the Solar to &quot;experiment&quot; in their chosen field without expending their mental resources. Once per day, the Solar may attempt a Major project using their chosen craft(s) without paying silver xp, though all other requirements apply. This roll produces no finished product, even on a success. It represents a period of pure experimentation, where new forms are tested and old styles challenged simply to see what <i>can</i> be done. The Solar gains crafting XP from this action as normal.<br /> <br /> Thoughts and critiques welcome, though we haven't had a chance to test this in game yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1318-kindledradial","name":"kindledRadial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1318_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T07:32:58-08:00","id":842975,"title":"","content":"You really shouldn't have to buy it again for each individual field. Apart from that, if you're really bent on using the system as-is, that seems like a decent Charm.<br /> <br /> But I think trying to fix Craft by adding Charms is a doomed endeavour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T21:59:43-07:00","id":874264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Design Beyond Limit<br /> Not gonna rewrite this one. I think the final EX3 release will probably include a well-written rewrite that complies with the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems I overestimated Onyx Path.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any suggestions on how to rewrite DBL and Celestial Reforging Technique?<br /> <br /> Is it even worth it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T23:32:59-07:00","id":874296,"title":"","content":"I mean, remove the reference to Emerald/Sapphire/Adamant and I don't see a problem with the charm TBH.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T12:14:45-07:00","id":874771,"title":"","content":"Artifacts no longer have set numbers of Evocations, so the Charm doesn't actually do anything right now.<br /> <br /> PS: Made a small edit to Glorious Solar Chef; instill should've been inspire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T15:21:17-07:00","id":874934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=874771#post874771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Artifacts no longer have set numbers of Evocations, so the Charm doesn't actually do anything right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure they do. It's not a mechanical &quot;X dots = Y evocations&quot;, but the system doesn't freely permit you to just homebrew up additional evocation for your (existing) artifact and learn them too.<br /> <br /> Specifically, it says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Evocations vary in number and power from artifact to artifact. The more powerful an artifact (as indicated by its dot rating), the more powerful and numerous its Evocations tend to be, though there are no hard and fast guidelines. </div> </div> </div>So you take an existing Artifact 3, or homebrew an Artifact 3 and your ST approves it by eyeballing other Artifacts 3. Then later you want to make it more powerful, so you add Evocations using Design Beyond Limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T15:58:59-07:00","id":874966,"title":"","content":"Independently of it still having any function, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/869481-opp-please-read-design-beyond-limit-final-pdf-version?p=869563#post869563\">Holden has flat out said that it was supposed to have been cut</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T16:55:07-07:00","id":875003,"title":"","content":"&quot;Add three to an eyeballed number&quot; would be bad Charm space even if spending motes and xp to increase the number of things someone is allowed to buy was a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T18:01:44-07:00","id":875060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=874934#post874934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure they do. It's not a mechanical &quot;X dots = Y evocations&quot;, but the system doesn't freely permit you to just homebrew up additional evocation for your (existing) artifact and learn them too.<br /> <br /> Specifically, it says:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So you take an existing Artifact 3, or homebrew an Artifact 3 and your ST approves it by eyeballing other Artifacts 3. Then later you want to make it more powerful, so you add Evocations using Design Beyond Limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be an ad-hoc house rule, not rules text. You can't have a charm that adds more to an arbitrary number. That'd be ridiculous.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: And Lea confirms<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/869481-opp-please-read-design-beyond-limit-final-pdf-version?p=875090#post875090\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...090#post875090</a><br /> <br /> Charm was supposed to have been cut.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","user":"Jetstream","date":". 04-26-2016, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T21:11:55-07:00","id":875239,"title":"","content":"We know the charm was supposed to be cut. Sanctaphrax asked for ideas to rewrite it. So I gave one.<br /> <br /> I happen to think &quot;add 3 evocations to something that was balanced as an N-dot artifact&quot; is perfectly reasonable design space, especially since a lot of artifacts people use will be pre-published rather than campaign-specific homebrew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T11:30:47-07:00","id":875798,"title":"","content":"I can't really agree. Moonlit Huntress and Spring Razor are both 3-dot Artifact weapons, but the first has a single Evocation* and the second has <i>five</i>. Adding 3 to those numbers will not be equally balanced for both, because the number of Evocations is already a balance mechanism on how powerful said evocations are.<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:8px\">plus baseline artifact-specific power, which apparently are also called Evocations</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T12:14:07-07:00","id":875835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=875798#post875798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't really agree. Moonlit Huntress and Spring Razor are both 3-dot Artifact weapons, but the first has a single Evocation* and the second has <i>five</i>. Adding 3 to those numbers will not be equally balanced for both, because the number of Evocations is already a balance mechanism on how powerful said evocations are.<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:8px\">plus baseline artifact-specific power, which apparently are also called Evocations</span></div> </div> </div> </div>... sure it would, as long as those additional charms are at the same basic poer level. Moonlit Huntress has fewer evocations because it has built-in properties.<br /> <br /> Seriously guys this is not complicated. You can let people add evocations to weapons without blowing things up. One way to do so is via a charm. Nothing breaks if you just let the charm continue to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T13:54:57-07:00","id":875950,"title":"","content":"Nothing breaks but it is completely pointless. If I were doing it, I'd just let people add evocations. No charm necessary. They'd just have to justify it to me and spend the xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T00:38:24-07:00","id":876331,"title":"","content":"I'm with Jetstream on this one.<br /> <br /> I overstated my case last post. Made it sound more objective than it is; I think this is mostly a matter of taste. But the nice thing about being some random unpaid guy on the internet is that I can shamelessly pander to my own preferences.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I finished my exams today. So I might as well get cracking on the next, possibly final, draft of this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=823639#post823639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further edits I'm considering:<br /> <br /> -Weakening Thousand-Forge Hands, at least for low-end Artifacts. As-is, you can really crank out 2-dot Artifacts.<br /> -Having Dual Magus Prana require Divine Inspiration Technique or something in addition to its current prereqs. It shouldn't be an easy Charm to get.<br /> -Changing the weapon and armour creating Charms so that they've both got the same duration.<br /> -Rewriting Shattering Grasp to be feat-of-strength-based.<br /> -Using BlueWinds' increment terminology for Craftsman Needs No Tools.<br /> -Turning some of the specialization Charm chains into repurchases.<br /> <br /> Opinions would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Should also limit multiple activations of Omniscient Surveyor Meditiation.</div> </div> </div> </div>-Make an Evocation-affecting Charm or two.<br /> \u200b-Add <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5526_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5526\" data-vbnamecard=\"5526\">Steamfunk</a>'s temporary Artifact recipe idea. (Assuming they don't object.)<br /> -Add an acknowledgements section.<br /> -Set up a wiki page.<br /> -Maybe lower Ability requirements across the board. There's an uncomfortable number of Craft 5 Charms here.<br /> -Maybe let the social influence Craft Charms be used for cooking.<br /> -Maybe cut something. The Charm list is pretty long.<br /> -Or maybe make a secondary Charm list, and move some extraneous Charms there. Could also include the candle-making Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T09:25:46-07:00","id":876725,"title":"","content":"Feel free to add my idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T10:41:47-07:00","id":876781,"title":"","content":"I would let 2-dot artifacts be a thing you can really churn out. They can't be weapons so the power level here is pretty limited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T01:06:49-07:00","id":879970,"title":"","content":"Looking at the example Artifacts...yeah, nothing will break if someone makes four 2-dot Artifacts in a session.<br /> <br /> Done:<br /> <br /> -Dual Magus Prana now requires Divine Inspiration Technique.<br /> -Steamfunk's artifact recipe idea is now included in the artifact creation rules.<br /> -Craftsman Needs No Tools now uses increment terminology.<br /> -The second post now contains an acknowledgements section.<br /> -Sublime Cartography Technique, Life From The Workshop, and Stone Legion Construction/Mechanical Legion Construction have been turned into repurchases of their prerequisites. Made some small wording changes while I was at it.<br /> -Omniscient Surveyor Meditation is now once per story per area.<br /> <br /> To do:<br /> <br /> -Changing the weapon and armour creating Charms so that they've both got the same duration.<br /> -Rewriting Shattering Grasp to be feat-of-strength-based.<br /> -Make an Evocation-affecting Charm or two.<br /> -Set up a wiki page.<br /> -Maybe lower Ability requirements across the board. There's an uncomfortable number of Craft 5 Charms here.<br /> -Maybe let the social influence Craft Charms be used for cooking.<br /> -Maybe cut something. The Charm list is pretty long.<br /> -Or maybe make a secondary Charm list, and move some extraneous Charms there. Could also include the candle-making Charms.<br /> -Maybe require people to specify which body is real ahead of time when using DMP. Now that it's Indefinite, it doesn't need to be retroactive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T18:10:04-07:00","id":880630,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial, sans-serif\">Now for the Charm-writing portion of this revision. As always, feedback would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> Shattering Grasp</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 6m; Mins: Craft 5, Essence 1</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Mute</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Craftsman Needs No Tools</span></span><br /> \u200b<br /> This Charm supplements a feat of strength to break a crafted object or structure. It allows the Solar to use Craft in place of Athletics. If the attempt is successful, the Solar may take the target apart neatly instead of smashing it. In addition, if the Solar spends a few extra minutes performing the attempt, she doubles 8s on the roll and may attempt feats with a Strength minimum up to twice her Strength score.<br /> <br /> This Charm is fully compatible with Athletics Charms.<br /> <br /> <i>Not sure if this is balanced right. The original seemed to say that you could destroy almost anything immediately, but that makes a mockery of Athletics-based breaking so I'd rather not do that.</i><br /> <br /> Design Beyond Limit<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 10m, 1wp; Mins: Craft 4, Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Indefinite</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Crack-Mending Technique, Craftsman Needs No Tools</span></span><br /> <br /> The Solar spends (10 - Essence) hours reforging an Artifact with Evocations in her workshop. When she's done, the Artifact's wielder gains access to an additional Evocation from that Artifact that they qualify for for as long as the Solar keeps the mote cost of this Charm committed. At any time while this Charm is active, the Artifact's wielder may pay the xp cost of the Evocation to learn it permanently.<br /> <br /> This Charm may only be used once per Artifact per story.<br /> <br /> <i>Half training time remover, half Power-Awarding Prana. Charms like this always make a little nervous but I think this one is okay.</i><br /> <br /> Celestial Reforging Technique<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 15m, 2wp; Mins: Craft 5, Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Simple</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: None</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Design Beyond Limit</span></span><br /> <br /> The Solar spends (10 - Essence) hours reforging an Artifact or group of Artifacts with Evocations in her workshop. When she's done, she can dissolve any number of Evocations into experience and spend that experience to buy other, different, Evocations. At the Storyteller's discretion, the Solar may also make changes to the structure and themes of the Artifacts. These changes can't alter the basic effects of the Artifact (unless the Storyteller sees fit to make an exception) but can change the Evocations available to it.<br /> <br /> This Charm may only be used once per story. It may be activated alongside its prerequisite.<br /> <br /> <i>Solar Tony Stark should be able to reconfigure his armour. And if he kills the Mask of Winters, and forges the Deathlord's body into his suit, he should be able to get some ghostly Evocations by doing so.</i><br /> <br /> Consumption-Demanding Cuisine<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 4m; Mins: Craft 4, Essence 2</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Agnostic</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Glorious Solar Chef</span></span><br /> <br /> This Charm supplements an attempt to cook something. If the attempt succeeds, the Solar rolls (Charisma + Craft) and for as long as the food remains fresh anyone whose Resolve is overcome by the Solar's roll is compelled to eat the Solar's cooking as soon as they see or smell it. Resisting this influence costs 2wp. If the food belongs to someone else, is full of broken glass, contains human flesh, is probably poisoned, or is otherwise obviously dangerous or unethical to eat, characters get +2 to their Resolve to avoid eating it and need only spend 1wp to resist the influence.<br /> <br /> If this Charm is activated alongside its prerequisite, use a single roll for both. A character who resists a use of this Charm is immune to it for the rest of the day.<br /> <br /> <i>I decided against extending the art Charms to cooking because I liked this idea better. The bit about dangerous or unethical food is mostly there to make it clear that yes, you can poison someone's food right in front of them and they might still eat it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a>, I suspect you might find this Charm, and the following one, interesting.</i><br /> <br /> Mind-Shattering Culinary Perfection<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Craft 5, Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Supplemental</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Agnostic</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Instant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Glorious Solar Chef</span></span><br /> <br /> This Charm supplements an attempt to cook something. If the attempt is successful, the resulting food is delicious enough to turn a man into a babbling mess. The Solar rolls (Charisma + Craft) and compares their result to the Resolve of anyone who eats it. Any character whose Resolve is overcome must spend 2wp or be rendered insensate by the sheer perfection of the Solar's cooking. Such a character gains a Defining Intimacy reflecting joy, admiration for the Solar, love of whatever food they ate, or something similar. He can take no useful action unless attacked. At the end of the hour, the Intimacy is reduced to the Major level and he may act normally once again. At the end of the day, it becomes Minor, and from then on it's a normal Intimacy.<br /> <br /> If this Charm is activated alongside its prerequisite, use a single roll for both.<br /> <br /> <i>Heavily inspired by <a href=\"http://www.girlgeniusonline.com/comic.php?date=20070620#.Vyf4-vkrLIV\" target=\"_blank\">this bit</a> from Girl Genius.</i><br /> <br /> Forge of the Sun<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost: -; Mins: Craft 5, Essence 3</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Type: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords: Agnostic</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration: Permanent</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites: Glorious Solar Arsenal, Glorious Solar Armoury</span></span><br /> <br /> This Charm enhances its prerequisites, increasing their duration to Indefinite. In addition, it allows the Solar to create multiple weapons or suits of armour with a single activation of either, paying 5m per weapon and 10m per suit of armour. The Solar may even create ammunition while doing so, paying 1m per shot and creating the first piece of ammunition within the weapon it's intended for.<br /> <br /> <i>This will be accompanied by a change to Glorious Solar Armoury, reducing its duration to One Scene.</i><br /> <br /> To do:<br /> <br /> -Add new Charms to list.<br /> -Add baking, etc, options to cooking Charms.<br /> -Set up a wiki page.<br /> -Maybe lower Ability requirements across the board. There's an uncomfortable number of Craft 5 Charms here.<br /> -Maybe cut something. The Charm list is pretty long.<br /> -Or maybe make a secondary Charm list, and move some extraneous Charms there. Could also include the candle-making Charms.<br /> -Maybe require people to specify which body is real ahead of time when using DMP. Now that it's Indefinite, it doesn't need to be retroactive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T18:21:28-07:00","id":880637,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, thanks for the cooking ideas. I can see a couple of those working, I might show them to my ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T12:49:09-07:00","id":881182,"title":"","content":"I didn't really feel like Shattering Grasp was overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T15:20:39-07:00","id":881300,"title":"","content":"I dunno if I'd call it overpowered, exactly. The original is kind of vague, but in a vacuum I wouldn't have a real problem with it.<br /> <br /> The issue only really arises when you try to fit it in alongside feat of strength Charms. If a Strength 1 character can easily go through stone walls and portcullises with a cheap low-level Craft Charm, and a Strength 5 character with a bunch of strength-focused Athletics Charms can't, it seems like a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T21:36:07-07:00","id":882529,"title":"","content":"These are fabulous. Gotten any further along with them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T23:30:54-07:00","id":882607,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <br /> I've decided to make DMP non-retroactive. 2e got a lot of flak for having Solve This Story Technique Charms, and retroactive DMP is basically Cleverly Escape From This Predicament Prana.<br /> <br /> And really, the ability to make Doombots is totally worth a Charm purchase.<br /> <br /> Also, I remember some people thought Perfect Gemcutter's Art seemed weak. Do y'all think making the light count as sunlight would be a good idea? How about making it inimical to creatures of darkness, like the light of the Simarils?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T12:59:33-07:00","id":883134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=882607#post882607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I remember some people thought Perfect Gemcutter's Art seemed weak. Do y'all think making the light count as sunlight would be a good idea? How about making it inimical to creatures of darkness, like the light of the Simarils?</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, can I say how much I love your Charm set; really inspiring and useful. Secondly, for Perfect Gemcutter's Art, how about adding an extra along the lines of: +3 Essence, the Solar can add a Minor Intimacy upon the gem at creation that affects anyone who wears or uses an item with the gem set. <br /> <br /> Once again, loving the thread.<br /> <br /> ~FC.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11718-forn-clakes","name":"Forn Clakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T02:50:43-07:00","id":883615,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <br /> Mixed feelings about that suggestion. On one hand, it's definitely useful. On the other, I'm not sure if it really fits into a gemcutting Charm. Gemcutting's not really a social art, is it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T10:35:10-07:00","id":883888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=883615#post883615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks!<br /> <br /> Mixed feelings about that suggestion. On one hand, it's definitely useful. On the other, I'm not sure if it really fits into a gemcutting Charm. Gemcutting's not really a social art, is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be more Larceny or something social, but maybe something that makes people extra-covetous of it? Sure, any superbly made item from a solar is gonna garner attention from people, but jewelry in particular seems to have a bit more &quot;object of desire&quot; to it. Might be a good way to set traps for thieves, bargain with merchant-princes, sow discord in a court and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T12:33:23-07:00","id":883987,"title":"","content":"That could be interesting. Maybe everyone who sees the gem could be treated as having a minor Intimacy of desire for it while it was present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T23:14:48-07:00","id":884408,"title":"","content":"Alright, I added the new Charms and edited DMP.<br /> <br /> I've decided not to lower the Ability requirements. At least not right now. If I ever do that, I should do it to the whole Charmset. Not just to one Ability.<br /> <br /> Looking at the Charm list, I like most of the Charms too much to get rid of them. Not so sure about Tireless Workhorse Method, Gaze of the Great Maker, and Breach-Healing Method, though. Maybe I should move those to a secondary list with the candle-making Charms and The Map Is The Territory.<br /> <br /> Advice would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> To do:<br /> <br /> -Set up a wiki page.<br /> -Decide what to do with Perfect Gemcutter's Art.<br /> -Maybe make a secondary Charm list, and move some extraneous Charms there. Could also include the candle-making Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T09:42:50-07:00","id":886350,"title":"","content":"Alright, how's this look?<br /> <br /> It's kind of mixture of the suggestions I received.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perfect Gemcutter's Art<br /> Cost: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Craft 4, Essence 1<br /> Type: Supplemental<br /> Keywords: Agnostic<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisites: Flawless Handiwork Method, a specialty in gemcutting<br /> <br /> This Charm supplements an attempt to cut and polish a gem. If the attempt is successful, the gem shines with light from within. The brightness of the glow depends on the value of the gem; a flawed quartz might only glow visibly in the dark, while a large and flawless diamond might be painful to look at. Gems cut this way glow until destroyed. If the gem would be worth at least Resources 4 without this magic, then it becomes so obviously intrinsically valuable that everyone in its presence is treated as though they had a minor Intimacy of desire for it or of admiration for its beauty. Resisting this effect costs 1wp. </div> </div> </div>And here's my plan for what's left to do:<br /> <br /> -Put Awe-Inspiring Feats of Craft, Gaze of the Great Maker, Tireless Workhorse Method, The Map Is The Territory, the candle-making Charms, the Sidereal Charms, and the Lunar Charms in a secondary document with a bunch of suggestions for further Charms and my discussions of what the crafting of other splats might look like.<br /> -Remove the comments from the rest, and provide full writeups even for the Charms I didn't change.<br /> -Pretty up the formatting and maybe add some flavour text.<br /> -Combine the Solar Charms and the base rules into a primary document.<br /> -Add both documents to the wiki, and make both available for easy downloading.<br /> <br /> Sound good?<br /> <br /> If not, now's your chance to speak up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T09:59:12-07:00","id":886369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=886350#post886350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">provide full writeups even for the Charms I didn't change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be sure, you may want to check if this is OK","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:16:24-07:00","id":886387,"title":"","content":"Irked already did that. As long as I don't actually duplicate the text, there should be no problem.<br /> <br /> Any comments on the Charm or the rest of the plan? The part I'm most hesitant about is the division of Charms between the documents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T10:38:59-07:00","id":886417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=886387#post886387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irked already did that. As long as I don't actually duplicate the text, there should be no problem.<br /> <br /> Any comments on the Charm or the rest of the plan? The part I'm most hesitant about is the division of Charms between the documents.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I'm only interested in the stuff you plan to place on the primary document, so it works for me ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T15:20:08-07:00","id":889392,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Pgj4L-Rmv2BK3efYhq6JAJx63WTI4k2q0IrlTi3KDZk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1YndQxorczy53pcrbp3XNiv8aruwL9XConywI7oc4iN8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Appendix</a><br /> <br /> In the end I didn't do add flavour text or do much with the formatting. I thought about it, and realized that probably nobody cares. And I didn't have any good formatting ideas anyway.<br /> <br /> I did make some small edits to Chaos-Resistance Preparation and Crack-Mending Technique, in the former case because I chose the BlueWinds version over the canon version and in the latter case because, while trying to transcribe the canon effect in different words, I found that I wasn't quite sure exactly what the canon effect was.<br /> <br /> Please let me know what you think of these. If they pass muster with y'all, I'll add them to the wiki and call this project complete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T00:30:02-07:00","id":893100,"title":"","content":"After some feedback from the SufficientVelocity crowd, I made a last round of changes to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Pgj4L-Rmv2BK3efYhq6JAJx63WTI4k2q0IrlTi3KDZk/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">the rewrite</a> and <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1YndQxorczy53pcrbp3XNiv8aruwL9XConywI7oc4iN8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">its appendix</a>.<br /> <br /> -Magic candles can now be ignited or extinguished mentally.<br /> <br /> -DMP now requires you to be within 3000 miles.<br /> <br /> -Art charms can now be used with visual art in general.<br /> <br /> -The Map Is The Territory now requires some form of ownership and costs more.<br /> <br /> -Added people to the acknowledgements.<br /> <br /> I'm ready to call this thing done, now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-18T00:55:08-07:00","id":893106,"title":"","content":"Oh hey I'm in there! Thanks, and this is great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T14:46:46-07:00","id":896316,"title":"","content":"You're welcome and thanks.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I finally got around to adding this to <a href=\"http://exalted3e.wikidot.com/houserules\" target=\"_blank\">the wiki</a>. Should've done that before calling the project finished...anyway, I think it's truly complete now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T23:37:38-07:00","id":931852,"title":"","content":"Now I have some time to spare after my first session, I can sink my teeth into this! Apologies if I repeat anything, I haven't been through the thread, and this is from the perspective of not having played through the crafting rules in-game, and with only having built one crafter PC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Fixing Craft</b><br /> <br /> <b>The tweaks:</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly onboard with these. Exceptions and comments to follow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Expand your definition of a &quot;Project&quot; to include anything that might provide inspiration for crafting. Discussing the design of a castle with fellow architects can be a Basic Project. Making a scale model of a manse can be a Major Project. Experimenting with chemicals, teaching an apprentice, studying a behemoth whose powers you want to emulate...they can all be Projects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm at a bit of a loss as to what this is meant to help, particularly as architecture is potentially now shoehorned into Basic Projects. I don't see designing large-scale structures as being that simple. Maybe there's a category mistake in my thinking - that structure design IS simple, it just needs specialised knowledge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. Craft is one ability, divided into areas of expertise the same way Lore is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes total sense, as Craft is otherwise a huge XP sink. Apart from the &quot;like Lore&quot; bit. Going on Stephen's comments in the Not-Quite-Newb thread, Lore gets a specialisation to reflect the person's education, with areas of expertise represented by specialities. For example, a graduate over here might have Law (Harvard), with specialities in Criminal Law, Copyright Law and International Human Rights Law. Things like Lore (dynast education) is apparently a thing. I can't see how craft could work in the same way, unless it's simply &quot;you get a free speciality when you purchase Craft dots for the first time, and need a relevant speciality to attempt a Craft roll at all&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. First Age wonders are just really powerful artifacts. Repairing them will often take odd components, but that's because you need appropriate materials to repair anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I... took this as read anyway. Or are you explicitly ditching any reference to First Age stuff in-system? Again, I almost took this as read, but the core seems to be building them differently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7. Steal the &quot;assess item&quot; action from the full rewrite below. (You can probably do this by the book, but I want to put some emphasis on it.)<br /> <br /> 8. Look over the Charms I've written and take some that have the Agnostic keyword. Maybe change the names, if necessary.<br /> <br /> 9. Look over the Charms in the book and ditch any that you don't want to play with.</div> </div> </div> </div>My first thought on reading this was &quot;clever, a gateway drug into the hard stuff you're offering&quot;. But I'm overly cynical, I feel. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10. Replace the &quot;When finishing your project upholds, furthers, or protects one of your character\u2019s Intimacies&quot; objective with &quot;When finishing your project involves roleplaying your character in an entertaining and appropriate way&quot;.<br /> <br /> 11. Replace the &quot;When finishing your project produces a clear in-game gain for your character&quot; objective with &quot;When finishing your project moves the story forward or opens up interesting possibilities for future play&quot;.<br /> <br /> 12. Replace the &quot;When finishing your project causes another character to gain or strengthen an Intimacy toward you&quot; with &quot;When finishing your project provides character development to another character or illustrates an interesting detail of the setting&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is kind of the intent of the original text of the game as written. RAW just implies that the plot of the game should be about adding roleplaying depth and motivation through a character's intimacies, whereas your adjustments make that more explicit. I guess I just see much of these as being almost two sides of the same coin, with your rules being less about systems engagement and more about direct engagement. But that said, I hugely dislike broad principles as intimacies and prefer to load up on ties, so I guess it's quite abusable in its way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Craft can also be used to assess crafted items. This is resolved with a (Perception + Craft) roll, with success allowing the crafter to determine how old an item is, how well it's made, what it's made of, and what condition it's in. A strong success may also allow the crafter to identify the maker if their style is distinctive.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes sense, but it makes Frugal Merchant Method pointless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character making a painting, a sculpture, or another emotionally-impactful object may attempt to encode a social influence attempt in it with (Charisma or Manipulation + Craft). Such influence must be vague, and must play on an Intimacy to do anything other than inspire emotion. Intimacies exploited by art are always considered to be Minor, and characters who don't possess the targeted Intimacy may react unpredictably; for example, a painting that uses love of the Realm to make people like you will likely make you unpopular among people who hate the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character can work on (Craft/2, rounded up) projects at once, making progress on them all at once by using the downtime required by one project to work on another. An Artifact or Manse counts as two projects, so Craft 3 is required to attempt one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this simplification, but it still enables mass production. I really don't like the &quot;work on everything at once&quot; mechanic, which this doesn't fix. It's still better than keeping track of vast numbers of slots, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only essence-wielders may attempt to create Artifacts and Manses. Doing so requires an extended roll. The difficulty, interval, and goal number are set by the rating of the Artifact or Manse, while the terminus is set by the crafter's available resources.[/FONT][/COLOR]<br /> <br /> Making a X-dot Artifact has a difficulty of Y, a goal number of Z...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is lovely. Nice and clear, with ACTUAL TARGETS! Although I'm still curious about non-artefact projects. Is a town a four- or five-dot artefact, for example?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made the difficulties increase so that Terrestrials and other weaker crafters could use magic that adds intervals to the Terminus. It seemed like an elegant way to push them towards smaller projects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although that assumes people will follow the logic of the system and not be &quot;I want to build THE BESTEST MANSE EVER, SCREW THE SYSTEM!&quot; as a Dragon-blooded. I'm always a little leery about systemic encouragement, despite my above comments on intimacies (I think that's one of the few examples where it actually works).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are no temporary or single-use Artifacts. However, there are Artifacts which serve only to create temporary or single-use magical items. For example, the recipe for a magical injury-healing soup could be an Artifact. The rating of such an Artifact depends on the power of the item created, how easily it can be used to create that item, and how often it can create that item. It's possible for this type of Artifact to take the form of pure information, which can easily be copied into any number of books. Information Artifacts are obviously more useful than physical objects, and as such they have higher ratings than similar non-information artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes sense I guess...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Groups that intend to use these rules should discuss beforehand whether they intend to pace Artifact completion rolls by time in setting or by time spent playing. The two methods roughly equalize if there's a story per season and three sessions per story.</div> </div> </div> </div>These feel like REALLY quick stories. My groups (regardless of game) never finish a plot in three sessions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These intervals don't assume any specific amount of work per day, but a character may only accumulate rolls towards one Artifact at a time and may only spend their rolls when they have a chance to sit down in their workshop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't this contradicted by the &quot;make progress on them all at once&quot; during downtime? Or if there is a difference, in that you only focus on story-relevant artefacts during stories? If so, this needs to be clarified.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moreover, a character may only accumulate rolls if they're making a good-faith effort to work on the Artifact when they get the chance. A character who spends two sessions (using the story-based intervals) or two months (using the time-based intervals) in prison can make four rolls on a two-dot Artifact the next time they have a chance to work on it. This represents the character thinking about and planning their creation while unable to work on it properly, and it's up to the ST how far it can be taken.</div> </div> </div> </div>*muttermuttermutterandthereIwashopingforsomethings ensiblelikehoursworkedsuggestionsmuttermuttermutte r*<br /> <br /> This isn't a problem with your system as such, but I cannot for the life of me understand why every craft system out there is allergic to the idea of concrete time requirements for projects. Hand-waving &quot;oh you spend a few hours a day on this and that&quot; just makes my skin crawl and make me want to hit things. And now I will stop before I start foaming at the mouth and ranting.<br /> <br /> Also, isn't the allowance of spending time while in prison or whatever a bit generous? I don't expect that Creation's prisons generally let you have exercise times, visiting hours or other such things of the modern prison system, including writing materials for the design process. I would expect a Craft equivalent of Mind-Scribing Method to enable that sort of thing, not for it to be assumed that people can just think things out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a bunch of unfinished Artifacts sitting around is cool, but you can't advance them all at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Explicitly contradicted by your downtime rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To find the terminus for an Artifact-creation roll, add together the factors for their workshop and their materials. If you're missing either, you can't even start. Then add bonuses for extra time taken, the help of others, complementary abilities, relevant magic, and anything else that seems appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice, but I got really confused by its positioning. This would flow better if placed under the costings, rather than going on a tangent about the kinds of thing that can and can't be created; finish the general system before discussing caveats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Workshop &amp; Material termini stuff</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Beautiful. Actually gives meaning to the terminus in craft rolls, rather than making an arbitrary roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If you use up all of your rolls, all is not lost. Just ask the ST what you have to do to earn another roll, and they'll tell you. Chances are it won't be easy.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Is there actually a fail condition here? I feel like that should give the chance of one, but then again &quot;ask the ST&quot; is a plot hook generator, so I'm not sure what removing or lessening the options to carry on the project would solve.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797632#post797632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Notes On Crafting Magic</b></span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">These make nice thematic sense, but I have no idea what Dragon Kings are. I also get the sense that &quot;like Solars but deathier&quot; won't quite be the whole of the Abyssal wheelhouse.</span></span></span><br /> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Will post up thoughts on the charms soon.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T20:15:10-07:00","id":932353,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the review, Xerxes. I'm glad that at least some parts of the system met with your approval.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=931852#post931852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm at a bit of a loss as to what this is meant to help, particularly as architecture is potentially now shoehorned into Basic Projects. I don't see designing large-scale structures as being that simple. Maybe there's a category mistake in my thinking - that structure design IS simple, it just needs specialised knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's meant to help people who don't see their characters as bothering with low-level work.<br /> <br /> And most buildings are still Major, even with tweak #1.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=931852#post931852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes total sense, as Craft is otherwise a huge XP sink. Apart from the &quot;like Lore&quot; bit. Going on Stephen's comments in the Not-Quite-Newb thread, Lore gets a specialisation to reflect the person's education, with areas of expertise represented by specialities. For example, a graduate over here might have Law (Harvard), with specialities in Criminal Law, Copyright Law and International Human Rights Law. Things like Lore (dynast education) is apparently a thing. I can't see how craft could work in the same way, unless it's simply &quot;you get a free speciality when you purchase Craft dots for the first time, and need a relevant speciality to attempt a Craft roll at all&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible that my understanding of the Lore rules is bad. But I figured you could say Craft (sculptor and stonemason) the same way you'd say Lore (Dynast education).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=931852#post931852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... took this as read anyway. Or are you explicitly ditching any reference to First Age stuff in-system? Again, I almost took this as read, but the core seems to be building them differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. There's this weird thing in core about First Age Wonders, and I want to ditch that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=931852#post931852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first thought on reading this was &quot;clever, a gateway drug into the hard stuff you're offering&quot;. But I'm overly cynical, I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. That's not really how I think of it. It's just that I did my best to improve the system, so I'm gonna stick my attempted improvements anywhere they seem appropriate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=931852#post931852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this is kind of the intent of the original text of the game as written. RAW just implies that the plot of the game should be about adding roleplaying depth and motivation through a character's intimacies, whereas your adjustments make that more explicit. I guess I just see much of these as being almost two sides of the same coin, with your rules being less about systems engagement and more about direct engagement. But that said, I hugely dislike broad principles as intimacies and prefer to load up on ties, so I guess it's quite abusable in its way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no clue what the intent of the game as written is. But if the tweak makes the text and the intention the same, then that's a good thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=931852#post931852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This makes sense, but it makes Frugal Merchant Method pointless.</div> </div> </div> </div>It already was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=931852#post931852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love this simplification, but it still enables mass production. I really don't like the &quot;work on everything at once&quot; mechanic, which this doesn't fix. It's still better than keeping track of vast numbers of slots, though.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Isn't this contradicted by the &quot;make progress on them all at once&quot; during downtime? Or if there is a difference, in that you only focus on story-relevant artefacts during stories? If so, this needs to be clarified.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Explicitly contradicted by your downtime rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you look again, you'll see that you can only have 3 projects max and an artifact counts as 2. So you can only ever work on one artifact.<br /> <br /> Wording's weird and seems inconsistent because I edited the rules after writing some of those lines. Should probably edit that one of these days.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=931852#post931852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is lovely. Nice and clear, with ACTUAL TARGETS! Although I'm still curious about non-artefact projects. Is a town a four- or five-dot artefact, for example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> <br /> Non-artifact projects don't use these rules. You can't really fail to build a town, you know? You can always keep trying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=931852#post931852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although that assumes people will follow the logic of the system and not be &quot;I want to build THE BESTEST MANSE EVER, SCREW THE SYSTEM!&quot; as a Dragon-blooded. I'm always a little leery about systemic encouragement, despite my above comments on intimacies (I think that's one of the few examples where it actually works).</div> </div> </div> </div>They're welcome to try. I've set the rules up to stop them from succeeding, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=931852#post931852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These feel like REALLY quick stories. My groups (regardless of game) never finish a plot in three sessions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth is, I mostly play PbP. I have only a loose idea of how long stories are in session terms. Book says stories can take several sessions, so I went with 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=931852#post931852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*muttermuttermutterandthereIwashopingforsomethings ensiblelikehoursworkedsuggestionsmuttermuttermutte r*<br /> <br /> This isn't a problem with your system as such, but I cannot for the life of me understand why every craft system out there is allergic to the idea of concrete time requirements for projects. Hand-waving &quot;oh you spend a few hours a day on this and that&quot; just makes my skin crawl and make me want to hit things. And now I will stop before I start foaming at the mouth and ranting.<br /> <br /> Also, isn't the allowance of spending time while in prison or whatever a bit generous? I don't expect that Creation's prisons generally let you have exercise times, visiting hours or other such things of the modern prison system, including writing materials for the design process. I would expect a Craft equivalent of Mind-Scribing Method to enable that sort of thing, not for it to be assumed that people can just think things out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Concrete time requirements would seem a bit weird given the varied natures of artifacts and the general looseness of narrative time. I dislike imposing precision that I don't have to impose, especially when I know it will be ignored.<br /> <br /> And I guess that might've been too generous. Don't really remember why I went that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=931852#post931852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice, but I got really confused by its positioning. This would flow better if placed under the costings, rather than going on a tangent about the kinds of thing that can and can't be created; finish the general system before discussing caveats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that probably would've been a good idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=931852#post931852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[COLOR=#222222][FONT=arial]Is there actually a fail condition here? I feel like that should give the chance of one, but then again &quot;ask the ST&quot; is a plot hook generator, so I'm not sure what removing or lessening the options to carry on the project would solve.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fail condition is &quot;the ST asks you for something you're unable to manage&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=931852#post931852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">These make nice thematic sense, but I have no idea what Dragon Kings are. I also get the sense that &quot;like Solars but deathier&quot; won't quite be the whole of the Abyssal wheelhouse.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Lizard men with elemental powers. They were the world's dominant race and the chosen people of the Sun before the Exalted were created.<br /> <br /> And hopefully. But it'll definitely be in there, and it's the best I've got for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T13:39:29-07:00","id":935236,"title":"","content":"I finally have some time to look at the charms! Note that in the interest of post length, I'll only be calling out things that I am uncertain about, disagree with or answers a question that you put in the post. So apologies if this feels all confrontational - silence is agreement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=797637#post797637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Agnostic keyword indicates that the Charm with it functions equally well under the original rules or my rewritten rules. Most of them are aimed at giving people something non-Artifact-related to do with Craft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huzzah! Probably stealing them for my own table, even if I don't use this system wholesale.<br /> The rest of this post is now taken from the updated version.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Supreme Masterwork Focus</b><br /> This Charm may be repurchased at Craft 5 Essence 2+. This allows the Solar to spend an additional point of willpower to double 8s on a Craft roll instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be because I didn't read your complete rewrite afresh, but I did a double-take thinking &quot;what's happened to the gold point?&quot; On rereading your rewrite, you don't actually mention anywhere that you're ditching craft points. Or are you? I assume so, but the rewrite doesn't say either way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with the merit, each success counts as two dice from Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... any reason for making this count as two charm dice? I guess that the most common thing to do with this is to have mortals use it, so it probably won't come up, but is there a reason for effectively penalising Essence-users for using the example?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>I wanted to come up with a method of mass production that felt Solar.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>The pedant in me is saying &quot;well, it's probably more batch production or an assembly line really...&quot; Nevermind, ignore me.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shattering Grasp</b><br /> This Charm supplements a feat of strength to break a crafted object or structure. It allows the Solar to use Craft in place of Athletics. If the attempt is successful, the Solar may take the target apart neatly instead of smashing it. In addition, if the Solar spends a few extra minutes performing the attempt, she doubles 8s on the roll and may attempt feats with a Strength minimum up to twice her Strength score.<br /> This Charm is fully compatible with Athletics Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lovely system adjustment. But I'm not entirely sure why it should be compatible with Athletics charms. If disassembly is done through knowledge and not strength, why do things that bolster feats of strength give bonuses to that? And if that's the case, are there any that would give bonuses to the roll at all? I'm struggling to think of things.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Master Craftsman's Eye</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This charm has no duration. Given Gaze of the Great Maker (the point where I noticed this), I'd imagine it's around one action or so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Arete-Shifting Prana</b><br /> Upon purchasing this Charm, the Solar gains two additional Craft specialties for each Craft specialty they have. Further specialties may be purchased for 1xp, and take one third of the normal time to train.</div> </div> </div> </div>This a little too good on a first read, as it's effectively an xp multiplier, which isn't an effect I've seen anywhere else. Although limiting it to specialities shouldn't make things too terrible, as you say. It might just be a matter of taste. I can however see it being a problem if you have 2 crafters in a group - that sort of set-up kind of needs niche protection.<br /> <br /> Regardless of my liking of it, I think it needs renaming - it's not so much Arete-Shifting as Arete-Multiplying now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Awe-Inspiring Feats Of Craft</b><br /> A character who wishes to resist this may do so at no cost, but most people don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels fuzzy. Leaves the question &quot;why would anyone want to?&quot; unanswered. Perhaps rephrase to &quot;A character with a reason to resist this may do so at no cost&quot;, or &quot;A character with an existing intimacy that would contradict the new intimacy does not form one&quot;. That shifts the reason for its dismissal from ST fiat to character motivation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Craft Of War</b><br /> While this Charm is active, the Solar may use Dexterity + Craft to &quot;attack&quot; when attempting gambits. The Solar doubles 10s on the Initiative roll when doing so. Gambits enacted with this Charm represent battlefield applications of the Craft skill, and as such some gambits are not possible with this Charm while others are not possible without it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really like this idea, but I think this language could be a bit tighter. Instead of &quot; the Solar may use Dexterity + Craft to 'attack' when attempting gambits&quot;, change to &quot;the Solar may make craft gambits using Dex + Craft in place of their initial decisive attack dice pool&quot;. A bit more wordy, but it feels clearer to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Words As Workshop Method</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I like this charm, but the book version has a place as well. I don't think it should be a replacement, but an addition. Even if it's kept, I think it needs a different name. The Solar's words aren't the workshop, they are the workmanship.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Not sure about the costing </i><i>here</i><i>.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not either, it seems to be a bit pricy at the high end, but I don't have the maths to provide a reasonable set of alternatives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Breach-Healing Method</b><br /> This bonus does not apply to Shape Sorcery or Sorcerous Working rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any reason for this exclusion? Part of the return of the wonders of the First Age is better sorcery, surely?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Design Beyond Limit</b><br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp; Mins: Craft 4, Essence 2</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the same cost as the original, with less evocations given. This makes things feel a bit weird, but the ability to use it without the xp cost possibly justifies that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>First Movement Of The Demiurge</b></div> </div> </div> </div>What was the actual change here? Just the specification of artefact or manse?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Celestial Reforging Technique</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I assume that leaving out the XP cost is intentional? Also, not sure that leaving out the reforging of others' evocations is intentional either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i><i>Gemcutters might also get a Charm for destroying Hearthstones quickly and easily, or for modifying the effect that a Hearthstone provides.</i></i></div> </div> </div> </div>What about a jeweller charm that imparts intimacies on those who see it? The most obvious application is the &quot;as soon as I sees it I wants it, because it's my birthday&quot; necklace from Night's Master and The Silmarillion, and some Germanic myth I can only half-remember, but if it's broadened it could be more useful. Although that is veering into artefact territory, unless you use an &quot;as long as the motes are committed&quot; condition or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Arrows Of The Dawn</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Is this for just the one arrow, or for a whole quiver? If for one arrow, it feels a bit pricy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Twilight Chemistry</b><br /> Sovereign Glue: A nearly perfect adhesive. It's waterproof, heatproof, lasts forever, can stick anything to anything, and requires a Strength 10+ difficulty 15 feat of strength to pull apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>But how long does it take to set?<br /> <br /> Also, thank you for not confusing chemistry and alchemy, as usually happens with fantasy alchemy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alkahest: A universal solvent</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't this be &quot;universal corrosive&quot; or something? People call water the universal solvent, and it doesn't eat through anything.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, unless stored in packaging that takes a miscellaneous action to open, the vial will break and expose its carrier to its effects whenever that carrier takes falling damage or more than six dice of bashing damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had to read this twice to realise it was talking about breaking before being used. Could do with rephrasing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It burns for only a few seconds, but gives off as much heat as a bonfire. If used in combat, it has the same statistics as Alkahest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not just a round of fire damage?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Living Statue Genesis/Clockwork Menagerie Technique.</b><br /> They use the statistics of the Walking Statue from page 500 of the backer PDF.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are in the rulebook in this place now, not just the backer PDF.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Miraculous Mapmaker Method</b><br /> The effectiveness of this Charm depends on the accuracy of the information provided. A false map will update falsely, preserving its errors. However, a Solar using this Charm has a near-perfect sense for the consistency of the geographical information they're working with. Tricking them into drawing a false map has a difficulty of their Perception + Craft.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about when the Solar makes a map with false information because they have a terrible sense of direction, have not been to the place for years, or have another reason to make an honest mistake in their cartography that is not based on deception? Do they get a sense they're drawing the wrong thing then?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Glorious Solar Arsenal</b><br /> They have no Evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glorious Solar Sabre has the option to add them as repurchases of the charm. I take it this was an intentional omission?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mind-Shattering Culinary Perfection</b><br /> Such a character gains a Defining Intimacy reflecting joy, admiration for the Solar, love of whatever food they ate, or something similar. He can take no useful action unless attacked. At the end of the hour, the Intimacy is reduced to the Major level and he may act normally once again. At the end of the day, it becomes Minor, and from then on it's a normal Intimacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of me wonders if the decline of the intimacy should be slowed or stopped based on the number of threshold successes on the roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=817343#post817343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Dual Magus Prana</b><br /> <i>Considered dropping this entirely, but I realized it was a great fit for this tree so I tried to include a version that avoided some of the original's issues. Not sure if I succeeded.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm happier that this isn't retroactive, at the very least. That and it actually has a kind-of logical progression now, which was my biggest issue with it before. It was in the efficiency tree, where you're working really hard at making stuff better, and all of a sudden you can create a perfectly functional simulacrum. This tree makes sense for it.<br /> <br /> Overall, I really like it. Every charm feels like it has a place and does something worthwhile, which is more than I could say for the original set. This feels lean and, although not quite intuitive (not sure any craft tree could be that) like it serves the narrative more than it does bean-counting. I will be endeavouring to persuade my wife to use it and rejig her character sheet around it for our current game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":497,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","user":"Xerxes","date":". 07-21-2016, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T22:41:37-07:00","id":935452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be because I didn't read your complete rewrite afresh, but I did a double-take thinking &quot;what's happened to the gold point?&quot; On rereading your rewrite, you don't actually mention anywhere that you're ditching craft points. Or are you? I assume so, but the rewrite doesn't say either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am. <br /> <br /> The complete rewrite is meant to be, well, complete. Anything not mentioned is not included.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... any reason for making this count as two charm dice? I guess that the most common thing to do with this is to have mortals use it, so it probably won't come up, but is there a reason for effectively penalising Essence-users for using the example?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't really penalize Essence-users, it just doesn't raise their Charm cap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lovely system adjustment. But I'm not entirely sure why it should be compatible with Athletics charms. If disassembly is done through knowledge and not strength, why do things that bolster feats of strength give bonuses to that? And if that's the case, are there any that would give bonuses to the roll at all? I'm struggling to think of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, I prefer things to be compatible. And anyway, you're still rolling Strength.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This charm has no duration. Given Gaze of the Great Maker (the point where I noticed this), I'd imagine it's around one action or so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oops. It's meant to be Instant. Fortunately the Google Doc has it right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This a little too good on a first read, as it's effectively an xp multiplier, which isn't an effect I've seen anywhere else. Although limiting it to specialities shouldn't make things too terrible, as you say. It might just be a matter of taste. I can however see it being a problem if you have 2 crafters in a group - that sort of set-up kind of needs niche protection.<br /> <br /> Regardless of my liking of it, I think it needs renaming - it's not so much Arete-Shifting as Arete-Multiplying now.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's basically mandatory for anyone who wants four or more specialities. But I'm okay with that.<br /> <br /> I think Craft is better niche-protected than most abilities, even with this around. A sculptor, a chef, an architect, and a swordsmith ought to be more different than four Awareness masters even if they share some incidental Craft abilities.<br /> <br /> I prefer to stick to existing names where possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This feels fuzzy. Leaves the question &quot;why would anyone want to?&quot; unanswered. Perhaps rephrase to &quot;A character with a reason to resist this may do so at no cost&quot;, or &quot;A character with an existing intimacy that would contradict the new intimacy does not form one&quot;. That shifts the reason for its dismissal from ST fiat to character motivation.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I don't really see the problem. Is there really a difference between a character with reason to resist and a character who wishes to resist?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really like this idea, but I think this language could be a bit tighter. Instead of &quot; the Solar may use Dexterity + Craft to 'attack' when attempting gambits&quot;, change to &quot;the Solar may make craft gambits using Dex + Craft in place of their initial decisive attack dice pool&quot;. A bit more wordy, but it feels clearer to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm reluctant to reword things now that the project's done, but you have a point. I'll think about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this charm, but the book version has a place as well. I don't think it should be a replacement, but an addition. Even if it's kept, I think it needs a different name. The Solar's words aren't the workshop, they are the workmanship.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like the book version. Charms should have effects, not vague suggestions of effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any reason for this exclusion? Part of the return of the wonders of the First Age is better sorcery, surely?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I don't remember.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, though, I don't think returning the wonders of the First Age is a worthy effect for a Charm. Gives that time period too much metaphysical weight to say that its traits are encoded into Solar magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the same cost as the original, with less evocations given. This makes things feel a bit weird, but the ability to use it without the xp cost possibly justifies that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, canon DBL doesn't actually let you use the Evocations. It just gives you permission to learn them.<br /> <br /> Still, this version might be overcosted. I've been thinking about cheapening it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was the actual change here? Just the specification of artefact or manse?</div> </div> </div> </div>I also changed the prerequisites, made sets of three 10s not apply, and edited the wording for clarity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that leaving out the XP cost is intentional? Also, not sure that leaving out the reforging of others' evocations is intentional either.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was and it wasn't. Will reword.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a jeweller charm that imparts intimacies on those who see it? The most obvious application is the &quot;as soon as I sees it I wants it, because it's my birthday&quot; necklace from Night's Master and The Silmarillion, and some Germanic myth I can only half-remember, but if it's broadened it could be more useful. Although that is veering into artefact territory, unless you use an &quot;as long as the motes are committed&quot; condition or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>As it happens, the most recent version of Perfect Gemcutter's Art (from the Google Doc) does something a lot like that. But an upgrade to make it more potent, at the cost of some committed motes, sounds like a pretty good idea to me. If I was still looking for more Charm ideas, I'd write it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this for just the one arrow, or for a whole quiver? If for one arrow, it feels a bit pricy.</div> </div> </div> </div>One arrow.<br /> <br /> I think 2m is a pretty good price for 1 die to hit and either 2 damage or double 10s.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how long does it take to set?<br /> <br /> Also, thank you for not confusing chemistry and alchemy, as usually happens with fantasy alchemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never really thought about it...a second or two, I guess. Should be impractical but not impossible to use with a gambit in battle.<br /> <br /> And you're welcome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't this be &quot;universal corrosive&quot; or something? People call water the universal solvent, and it doesn't eat through anything.<br /> <br /> I had to read this twice to realise it was talking about breaking before being used. Could do with rephrasing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a reference to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alkahest\" target=\"_blank\">the legendary Alkahest</a>.<br /> <br /> I'll give the wording another look.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not just a round of fire damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not coincidentally, Alkahest exposure is identical mechanically to a round of fire damage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are in the rulebook in this place now, not just the backer PDF.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I should edit that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about when the Solar makes a map with false information because they have a terrible sense of direction, have not been to the place for years, or have another reason to make an honest mistake in their cartography that is not based on deception? Do they get a sense they're drawing the wrong thing then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> Honest mistakes are never gonna be consistent enough with each other, or with accurate information, to go unnoticed while using this Charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glorious Solar Sabre has the option to add them as repurchases of the charm. I take it this was an intentional omission?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Didn't really feel appropriate to have Evocations for items you create on the fly.<br /> <br /> And Glorious Solar Armoury offers some stuff that Glorious Solar Sabre doesn't, so it should also not offer some stuff that Glorious Solar Sabre does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of me wonders if the decline of the intimacy should be slowed or stopped based on the number of threshold successes on the roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a bad idea, but I'd rather not make the Charm any more complicated than it already is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm happier that this isn't retroactive, at the very least. That and it actually has a kind-of logical progression now, which was my biggest issue with it before. It was in the efficiency tree, where you're working really hard at making stuff better, and all of a sudden you can create a perfectly functional simulacrum. This tree makes sense for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that bugged me too. Although not as much as the absolute invincibility of the Charm, or its &quot;story in a bottle&quot; effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall, I really like it. Every charm feels like it has a place and does something worthwhile, which is more than I could say for the original set. This feels lean and, although not quite intuitive (not sure any craft tree could be that) like it serves the narrative more than it does bean-counting. I will be endeavouring to persuade my wife to use it and rejig her character sheet around it for our current game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. I'm really glad you like it. Hope your wife does too.<br /> <br /> And thanks for the critique. It's helpful stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T09:28:21-07:00","id":935646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=935236#post935236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any reason for this exclusion? Part of the return of the wonders of the First Age is better sorcery, surely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerous Workings are unique in Exalted system design. Most systems in Exalted (past or present) have been splat-neutral, and between-splat variation has been handled through Charms that interact with the system (combined with normal dice caps). For example, Craft is heavily balanced in this fashion; the difficulties are the same for everyone, and the primary way the game expresses &quot;what feats are Solars capable of doing?&quot; is through the Power line of Charms that are effectively capbreakers.<br /> <br /> Sorcerous Workings are different; the <b>system itself</b> encodes &quot;what can DBs do; what can Lunars do; what can Solars do&quot; through the Circles and the dice caps. If you run the math you can actually see stuff like &quot;oh, a Dragon-blooded attempting an Ambition 3 Celestial working will need X means to succeed and will take Y months&quot;, and how this corresponds reasonably to what you would want the <i>actual</i> probabilities to be to be consistent with the setting as written*. You can see how the Lunars crafting their Destiny-warping-thingy over the Caul was a project they could plausibly do but only with a lot of time and effort: this is probably an Ambition 3 Solar Working, which would probably require about 8-10 Means and several years for an experienced Lunar sorcerer with maxed dicepools and applicable stunts on every roll.<br /> <br /> As a result of this, the actual design space of &quot;Charms to boost Workings rolls&quot; is not a good one.<br /> <br /> *they are a <i>little</i> too easy to be perfectly compatible but that's mostly due to the benefits of stunting, which I chalk up to PC exceptionalism","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T09:42:07-07:00","id":935650,"title":"","content":"Non-post, because I'm thick. The point makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":497,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","user":"Xerxes","date":".  Even more sudden-realisations 07-22-2016, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T06:29:02-07:00","id":1083439,"title":"","content":"Hello<br /> <br /> First of all, I'm a big fan of what you've done with craft. One of my player is a crafter and he enjoy this system too so we've decided to play with it.<br /> <br /> I have one question about &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First Movement Of The Demiurge&quot;. Does the transformation of a non-success to a 10 count for the limitation of adding dice to a roll ?<br /> <br /> I have another Question about probabilities. Consider a Crafter with Dex 5 and Supernal Craft 5. One roll with full excellencies will end in:<br /> <br /> 2 &quot;1&quot;, 2 &quot;2&quot;, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2 &quot;3&quot;, 2 &quot;4&quot;, 2 &quot;5&quot;, 2 &quot;6&quot;, 2 &quot;7&quot;, 2 &quot;8&quot;, 2 &quot;9&quot; and 2 &quot;10&quot;<br /> <br /> If he have all the &quot;optimization&quot; charms, that means:<br /> <br /> 1) 16 success (because of the Double 7's) + 4 reroll for the 2 &quot;6&quot; and 2 &quot;10&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) The 4 reroll will give him 2 more success which raise the number of success to 18 success and great chance of having a set of 3 &quot;7&quot;, &quot;8&quot; or &quot;9&quot;<br /> <br /> 3) </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So he can roll 18/3 = 6 more dice which give him 4 more success<br /> <br /> 4) He could eventually get another set of 3 </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;7&quot;, &quot;8&quot; or &quot;9&quot;, that means, with the first one, 2 &quot;1&quot; transformed in 2 &quot;10&quot; so 4 more success and 2 reroll (maybe 3 because of the possible &quot;6&quot; rolled in step 2) or 3) )</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5) With the 3 reroll he gets 2 more success, that means 6/3 = 2 more dice<br /> <br /> 6) The 2 more dice means 2 success<br /> <br /> Total = 30 success<br /> <br /> That means 3 or 4 Craft roll to achieve a 5 dot Artifact. Am I right ?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12575-gaara","name":"Gaara","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T09:14:34-07:00","id":1083489,"title":"","content":"So, Sanctaphrax can't actually post in this thread anymore (because he's been banned); you might try the forums over at Sufficient Velocity if you want a detailed answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T10:09:24-07:00","id":1084042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=1083439#post1083439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello<br /> <br /> First of all, I'm a big fan of what you've done with craft. One of my player is a crafter and he enjoy this system too so we've decided to play with it.<br /> <br /> I have one question about &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First Movement Of The Demiurge&quot;. Does the transformation of a non-success to a 10 count for the limitation of adding dice to a roll ?<br /> <br /> I have another Question about probabilities. Consider a Crafter with Dex 5 and Supernal Craft 5. One roll with full excellencies will end in:<br /> <br /> 2 &quot;1&quot;, 2 &quot;2&quot;, </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">2 &quot;3&quot;, 2 &quot;4&quot;, 2 &quot;5&quot;, 2 &quot;6&quot;, 2 &quot;7&quot;, 2 &quot;8&quot;, 2 &quot;9&quot; and 2 &quot;10&quot;<br /> <br /> If he have all the &quot;optimization&quot; charms, that means:<br /> <br /> 1) 16 success (because of the Double 7's) + 4 reroll for the 2 &quot;6&quot; and 2 &quot;10&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) The 4 reroll will give him 2 more success which raise the number of success to 18 success and great chance of having a set of 3 &quot;7&quot;, &quot;8&quot; or &quot;9&quot;<br /> <br /> 3) </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So he can roll 18/3 = 6 more dice which give him 4 more success<br /> <br /> 4) He could eventually get another set of 3 </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">&quot;7&quot;, &quot;8&quot; or &quot;9&quot;, that means, with the first one, 2 &quot;1&quot; transformed in 2 &quot;10&quot; so 4 more success and 2 reroll (maybe 3 because of the possible &quot;6&quot; rolled in step 2) or 3) )</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5) With the 3 reroll he gets 2 more success, that means 6/3 = 2 more dice<br /> <br /> 6) The 2 more dice means 2 success<br /> <br /> Total = 30 success<br /> <br /> That means 3 or 4 Craft roll to achieve a 5 dot Artifact. Am I right ?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>If you are just asking &quot;does changing a die to a 10 count against my dice cap?&quot; the answer is no.<br /> <br /> The rest of your math starting with item 3 doesn't really follow, and also your general strategy of trying to measure the value of FMotD through a uniform spread of die results isn't going to give a good answer, since much FMotD's value comes in the variance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T23:00:01-07:00","id":1084351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=1083489#post1083489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Sanctaphrax can't actually post in this thread anymore (because he's been banned); you might try the forums over at Sufficient Velocity if you want a detailed answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>How'd he get banned, anyways?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T23:29:30-07:00","id":1084357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PlotVitalNPC</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it?p=1084351#post1084351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How'd he get banned, anyways?</div> </div> </div> </div>He basically confronted Rich in an issue on a thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T23:34:51-07:00","id":1084359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/